From: Marionette AirDrop driver research
Subject: [EXPERIMENTAL] compare RAW firmware RX resources with Ethernet STA vdevs

0021 explicitly configured monitor RX_DECAP RAW through the existing vdev
MLME/DP/WMI path, but still delivered no action/AWDL. Global monitor mode also
changes the earlier firmware resource RX decap default from Ethernet to RAW.
Under a new default-off load-time flag plus the existing STA-monitor gate,
use that same declared RAW resource value while keeping mission mode. Set
every STA vdev (including internal links) explicitly to Ethernet through the
same per-vdev API before association. Ordinary Wi-Fi is a prerequisite test.
No change to descriptor layouts, channel/regulatory checks, TX or firmware
images. This compares a documented initialization difference; actual mixed
format support and receipt remain unproven and require volatile rollback.

